From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Fri, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: ufs: add MT6873 host fallback

The MT6873 vendor UFS controller uses the same MMIO window and interrupt
model exposed by the MediaTek UFS host driver.  Describe an MT6873-specific
compatible with an MT8183 fallback so the integration can be tested without
claiming that every undocumented controller feature is equivalent.

This is a development binding for the atom bring-up branch, not evidence
that UFS link, PHY calibration, crypto, MCQ, or runtime PM are functional.

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/mediatek,ufs.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/mediatek,ufs.yaml
index 1dec54f..03397c0 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/mediatek,ufs.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/mediatek,ufs.yaml
@@ -10,10 +10,14 @@ maintainers:
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    enum:
-      - mediatek,mt8183-ufshci
-      - mediatek,mt8192-ufshci
-      - mediatek,mt8195-ufshci
+    oneOf:
+      - items:
+          - const: mediatek,mt6873-ufshci
+          - const: mediatek,mt8183-ufshci
+      - enum:
+          - mediatek,mt8183-ufshci
+          - mediatek,mt8192-ufshci
+          - mediatek,mt8195-ufshci
 
   clocks:
     minItems: 1
-- 
